    "body": "## Security impact\n\n`POST /payouts/{id}/cancel` previously loaded payout requests globally under a pessimistic lock and only then checked ownership. Because payout IDs are numeric, an authenticated outsider could distinguish an existing foreign payout (`403`) from a nonexistent payout (`404`). That leaks the existence of financial activity and creates an enumeration oracle over sensitive payout records.\n\n## Fix\n\n- add an owner-scoped pessimistic-write lookup for user-driven payout cancellation;\n- resolve cancellation by `(payoutId, authenticatedUserId)` before any state mutation;\n- return the existing neutral not-found response for both missing and foreign payout IDs;\n- fail closed if the authenticated user id is unavailable;\n- retain the global locked lookup for trusted provider/recovery flows that need system-wide access.\n\n## Financial correctness\n\nThe payout cancellation transaction, status guard, wallet source restoration, idempotent restoration operation key, and audit-event writes are unchanged after ownership resolution. The only behavioral change is removing the foreign-payout existence oracle.\n\n## Tests\n\n- owner cancellation still restores reserved funds and records both audit events;\n- outsider cancellation resolves only through the owner-scoped locked lookup;\n- outsider path cannot touch the global lock, wallet restoration, or event writes.",
